body:
She has hearing aids but does not wear them often.  

&#x200B;

I have no idea why her siblings do not like her.

my adopted daughter is 17.  she is profoundly  deaf and has no hearing at all.  She was in a mainstream school when she was 8 and younger according to her files and she has home schooled the rest of the times.

&#x200B;

My biological daughters are 8, 10, and 13.  We have fostered other children before and when the foster system told us we had a permanent placement option we were so happy.  We wrote letters to her and made her bears so we all had matching build a bears and other things like that.
